    "result": "`shipping_cost` is implemented in `solution.py`, and `python -m pytest -q tests` passes (9 tests). The tests are in `tests/test_solution.py`.\n\nThe function follows the spec rules and rounds with `ROUND_HALF_UP` only at the end. It validates inputs as the spec says (`TypeError` for non-numbers and bools, `ValueError` for out-of-range values and bad zones). The tests cover the rule boundaries, the validation cases and the two-decimal `Decimal` return type.\n\nMy first run had one failing test: I had written the wrong expected value for the 120 cm oversize boundary. The implementation was correct, and I fixed the test.\n\nThe spec doesn't cover `nan` or `inf` inputs, so I made them raise `ValueError`. That choice is untested.",
